# Day 51 – Product Discovery & Sprint Planning

## 60 Days of Claude AI Challenge

Today marks the beginning of the final 10-day Capstone Project of the 60 Days of Claude AI Challenge.

The focus of Day 51 was Product Discovery & Sprint Planning — moving from an initial idea toward a clearly defined and realistic v1.0 product that can be built and deployed within 10 days.

## What I Worked On

- Used Claude as a structured product discovery partner
- Explored and refined the project idea through guided questions
- Defined the scope of the v1.0 product
- Identified features to include and deliberately exclude
- Defined clear Day 10 success criteria
- Created a Product Requirements Document (PRD)
- Created an Implementation Blueprint for Days 2–10
- Prepared a Project Pitch Deck

## Key Learnings

### 1. Guided Discovery
Learned how structured AI-led interviews can help identify and refine a strong, realistic project idea instead of immediately choosing the most ambitious option.

### 2. Scope Discipline
Understood the importance of clearly defining what v1.0 includes, what is excluded, and what a successful final product should look like.

### 3. Professional PRD
Learned how to create a Product Requirements Document that acts as a single source of truth throughout the development process.

### 4. Implementation Blueprint
Created a structured roadmap for the remaining days so that development can continue with clear goals and minimal re-planning.

## Deliverables

- Product Requirements Document (PRD)
- Implementation Blueprint
- Project Pitch Deck
- Project Scope and Success Criteria

## Key Takeaway

Building a successful product doesn't start with coding. It starts with understanding the right problem, defining a realistic scope, and creating a clear execution plan.

Day 51 begins the final 10-day journey from idea to a deployed v1.0 product.

